settings.py:28-30 `if env.get(key):
        return "env"
    if project.get(key):
        return "project"
    if user.get(key):
        return "user"` contradicts settings.py:6-7 `A layer "carries" a key when the key is present, whatever the value -- an explicitly empty string is a deliberate override, not an absence.` and settings.py:18-20 `if key in env:
        return env[key]`
